      "content": "that looks good, but we need to be more specific with the legal justifications. since the principality was dissolved under irregular circumstances during the wars, the standard treaties might not be enough to force their hand. what kind of precedent can we cite regarding 'de facto' sovereignty or the rights of non-territorial states to maintain diplomatic presence? i need the language to suggest that my claim isn't just a request, but an exercise of an existing, though suppressed, legal right.",
